WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:04.646
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.771 --> 00:08.191
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.316 --> 00:11.944
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.070 --> 00:14.155
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.863 --> 00:18.117
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.199 --> 00:23.330
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.330 --> 00:24.790
"Laugh and cry

00:24.873 --> 00:30.212
"He's a family guy

00:37.803 --> 00:40.096
Oh, my, this place is enormous.

00:40.221 --> 00:45.310
They got these plastic disc guns.
I haven't seen one since Cleveland's wedding.

00:45.435 --> 00:48.354
Dearly beloved, we are gathered here today

00:48.437 --> 00:51.274
to celebrate the joining
of these two people...

00:51.359 --> 00:55.652
...in the bonds of holy matrimony,

00:55.736 --> 00:58.864
consecrated before God Almighty.

00:59.406 --> 01:02.327
Hey, Stratego. I used to love this game.

01:02.327 --> 01:04.621
Oh, my God. Abe Vigoda?

01:04.621 --> 01:08.164
Go bother Steve Guttenberg.
He's behind the Chinese chequers.

01:08.164 --> 01:09.625
Abe, shut up!

01:15.340 --> 01:19.926
Look at me, Chris. I'm Yanni sans the attitude.

01:20.678 --> 01:23.055
My God, that's amazing.

01:23.180 --> 01:25.681
- You are so talented.
- Huh?

01:25.765 --> 01:28.892
Wait a second. Something's not right here.

01:29.017 --> 01:33.273
You were just making it look like
you were playing. You're a phony!

01:33.398 --> 01:37.359
- Hey! This guy's a great big phony!
- Come on, Chris.

01:40.071 --> 01:41.739
- Agh!
- There you are.

01:41.823 --> 01:44.659
Hey, you're a great big phony,
you know that?

01:44.659 --> 01:47.036
Your mom and I have something for you.

01:47.161 --> 01:49.955
Let me guess. Another
colourful box with a crank

01:50.080 --> 01:53.709
that I'm expected to turn until -
big shock - a jack pops out.

01:53.834 --> 01:59.256
And you laugh and the kids laugh and
the dog laughs and I die a little inside.

01:59.339 --> 02:02.176
Surprise, honey.

02:02.260 --> 02:04.344
A trikey!

02:04.885 --> 02:05.930
I think he likes it.

02:06.013 --> 02:10.726
When I stick this army guy with the sharp
bayonet up my nose, it tickles my brain.

02:10.808 --> 02:15.398
Ow! Oh. Now I don't know math.

02:16.647 --> 02:20.736
- Give it to me now, dammit!
- Not now, Stewie. When we get home.

02:20.736 --> 02:25.323
That's right. You're a big fat phony!

02:27.074 --> 02:32.080
What I'm about to show you is a fight scene
from Star Trek, season one, episode 18.

02:32.205 --> 02:37.292
I'm going to identify when it's Shatner and
when it's his stunt double, Fred Lubbins.

02:37.419 --> 02:38.461
Let's watch.

02:38.544 --> 02:42.422
That's Shatner. That's Lubbins.
That's Shatner. That's Lubbins.

02:42.422 --> 02:44.383
That's Shatner. That's Lubbins.

02:44.508 --> 02:49.514
That's Shatner, but when I freeze-frame,
you can clearly see Lubbins' coffee cup.

02:49.598 --> 02:52.641
- He is the biggest dork on the planet.
- Totally.

02:52.641 --> 02:55.977
And so, because of his
rough-and-tumble style of command,

02:55.977 --> 03:00.357
Captain Kirk is clearly superior
to Jean-Luc Picard.

03:00.357 --> 03:04.944
- Any questions? Meg?
- No. Leave me alone.

03:04.944 --> 03:07.949
Thank you, Neil,
for that irrelevant presentation.

03:08.074 --> 03:12.118
We all know Captain Picard
is the superior officer.

03:16.497 --> 03:20.377
- Ugh!
- Mr Lassenbee's getting arrested.

03:23.712 --> 03:28.092
What in God's name...? Mr Lassenbee,
what the hell's going on here?

03:28.092 --> 03:31.428
There's a law against teaching
the evolutionary theory

03:31.512 --> 03:35.891
that Gil Gerard used a time machine
and ejaculated into the primordial ooze.

03:36.016 --> 03:38.186
This stupid country.

03:38.311 --> 03:42.689
Tom Tucker, live at James Woods High
School with this sensational breaking story.

03:42.772 --> 03:47.694
A teacher caught molesting children...
with crackpot theories. Full story at 11.

03:47.694 --> 03:48.737
And out.

03:48.820 --> 03:51.864
Oh, my God!
That's Tom Tucker from the news.

03:51.864 --> 03:57.161
Hey, kids. Remember, Mr T says
"I pity the fool who does drugs. "

04:05.837 --> 04:09.048
- Better hurry up, Mr Tucker.
- I'm coming.

04:20.852 --> 04:24.271
Reports indicate she has consumed
a record amount of seamen.

04:24.396 --> 04:26.566
Sounds like one powerful hurricane.

04:26.691 --> 04:31.070
In other news, school board elections
took place last evening.

04:31.070 --> 04:35.449
Fred Johnson leads candidate Betsy LaFoe
by a substantial...

04:44.916 --> 04:48.169
Hi, Meg. You know how cute I think you are.

05:09.232 --> 05:12.777
...turmoil when President Bush
stuck his finger in a socket.

05:12.861 --> 05:14.029
Whoa!

05:14.111 --> 05:16.614
Yikes. Awkward.

05:16.738 --> 05:19.866
...that's where leprechauns
hide their gold. More at 11.

05:19.950 --> 05:25.497
Hey, you know who lives in this house?
A great big phony! That's right.

05:25.497 --> 05:29.543
A phony lives here. A big fat phony!

05:32.670 --> 05:35.924
I say, look at me.
I feel like a regular grease monkey.

05:36.008 --> 05:41.012
- Remember that time I had that Mustang?
- Oh, yeah, you took her for a spin that time.

05:41.137 --> 05:42.388
That was awesome.

05:42.471 --> 05:45.517
Those chowderheads on the corner
busted your stones.

05:45.599 --> 05:49.271
Hey, your sister say anything about me?

05:50.730 --> 05:54.275
- Oh, my God. I'm missing the news!
- We all miss The News, Meg.

05:54.359 --> 05:57.903
But Huey Lewis needs time to create.
We have to be patient.

05:58.029 --> 06:01.992
And in entertainment,
Mary Tyler Moore is 64 years old today.

06:01.992 --> 06:03.534
- Really? 64?
- Yes.

06:03.659 --> 06:05.829
- I thought she was dead.
- She's alive.

06:05.954 --> 06:07.913
Fantastic. And now this.

06:08.038 --> 06:12.417
Are you a student interested in
the glamorous world of unpaid internships?

06:12.417 --> 06:16.380
If so, you can try out for
Channel Five's young anchor programme.

06:16.464 --> 06:17.923
Oh, wow!

06:18.048 --> 06:21.592
You'll gain valuable experience,
work closely with Tom and me,

06:21.676 --> 06:23.970
and produce your own on-air report.

06:24.096 --> 06:25.138
So call us now.

06:25.221 --> 06:26.263
Yeah!

06:38.066 --> 06:41.613
Question number one:
Would you consider growing a moustache?

06:41.696 --> 06:43.073
I guess so.

06:43.073 --> 06:45.367
Question two: Look at my moustache.

06:45.367 --> 06:48.161
Do you think it tickles women
when I kiss them?

06:48.286 --> 06:49.328
I don't know.

06:49.411 --> 06:53.289
Wrong. The answer is: Only slightly,
only slightly. Next.

06:54.959 --> 06:58.088
Oh, God, I can't hire any of these girls.

06:58.171 --> 07:01.424
They're all too pretty.
Their breasts are too perky.

07:02.465 --> 07:03.509
Perfect.

07:03.593 --> 07:05.677
Congratulations. You got the job.

07:05.802 --> 07:10.808
Oh, my God! Oh, thank you, thank you!
This is beyond anything I've ever dreamed of!

07:10.891 --> 07:13.810
You and your partner
will start tomorrow after school.

07:13.934 --> 07:17.064
- Great! Who's my partner?
- Hey, there, hot stuff!

07:23.403 --> 07:28.406
Well, well. It appears the Fates
have conspired in our favour. Eh, Meg?

07:28.531 --> 07:31.868
Stay away from me, Neil.
Just because we're working together

07:31.868 --> 07:34.163
does not mean I like you. Give it to me!

07:34.247 --> 07:36.249
- What's that?
- Give it to me, Neil.

07:36.332 --> 07:41.879
- Give it to me! Give it to me, Neil.
- Yeah. That'll work just fine.

07:41.962 --> 07:42.713
Ugh!

07:42.798 --> 07:46.050
Look who's here.
It's our bright-eyed young interns.

07:46.134 --> 07:49.803
- Did you two wear your eager caps?
- I sure did, Mr Tucker.

07:49.803 --> 07:52.723
Great. Cos you two
are gonna have so much fun!

07:52.806 --> 07:55.935
Don't act any cheerier.
You'll give us all diabetes.

07:56.060 --> 07:58.853
- Bite me, Tom.
- Come on, kids.

07:58.978 --> 08:02.105
Here's where we produce
our celebrity interviews.

08:02.105 --> 08:05.944
I did one with Dustin Hoffman.
He's almost impossible to book.

08:06.069 --> 08:09.198
Dustin, it's been a while.
I gotta say, you look great.

08:09.281 --> 08:11.074
Are you trying to seduce me?

08:11.157 --> 08:15.536
I am not trying to seduce you,
Dustin Hoffman. You really look great.

08:15.661 --> 08:19.498
- Uh-oh. Twelve minutes to Wapner.
- I understand your hectic schedule.

08:19.623 --> 08:23.168
We appreciate you taking the time
to be with us here in the studio.

08:23.252 --> 08:27.006
- If there's anything I can ever do for you...
- Bring me Peter Pan!

08:27.131 --> 08:30.052
I'll keep my eye out for him.
Thanks, Dustin.

08:30.052 --> 08:31.927
He's this tall.

08:32.970 --> 08:37.141
Can you believe it? Our little Stewie
learning to ride his first tricycle.

08:37.141 --> 08:41.311
This'll be more exciting than when Brian
taught me about Columbus.

08:41.311 --> 08:44.439
- Where are we going?
- We're going to visit the year 1492.

08:44.439 --> 08:46.941
That's when Columbus set sail
for the New World.

08:47.024 --> 08:49.319
- We're on a ship.
- This is the Santa Maria.

08:49.443 --> 08:51.739
Columbus took it to find a route to India.

08:51.822 --> 08:54.324
- Any sign of India yet?
- Nothing yet.

08:54.449 --> 08:56.410
Columbus was going to America.

08:56.535 --> 08:59.246
Columbus discovered America
entirely by mistake.

08:59.329 --> 09:00.371
Wow!

09:00.914 --> 09:04.541
- What are you doing? Back off, fat man.
- Hang on, Stewie.

09:04.668 --> 09:07.878
What the...? Hey, hey, let go.
Get your filthy paws off.

09:08.003 --> 09:11.215
Let go. Let go, I say. Let go. Don't let go!

09:12.259 --> 09:13.925
Oh, this is exhilarating.

09:14.051 --> 09:16.553
- Go, Stewie!
- Yay, Stewie!

09:16.637 --> 09:20.723
I gotta go check on dinner. You keep
taping Stewie. Don't miss a moment.

09:20.723 --> 09:22.894
I got it.

09:23.018 --> 09:25.728
Look, it's dancing with me.

09:25.728 --> 09:29.483
It's this incredibly benevolent force
that wants me to know

09:29.483 --> 09:31.985
there's no reason to be afraid.

09:32.069 --> 09:36.782
Sometimes there's so much beauty
in the world, it makes my heart burst.

09:36.782 --> 09:39.283
It's just some trash blowing in the wind!

09:39.366 --> 09:43.245
Do you have any idea how complicated
your circulatory system is?

09:44.706 --> 09:49.794
Hi, Mr Tucker. I brought you Rice Crispy
Treats. I remember you said you liked them.

09:49.919 --> 09:52.421
Look. This one is in the shape of a heart.

09:52.504 --> 09:56.591
I'm sorry, but there's a handsome man
in my spoon. Come back later.

09:58.053 --> 10:02.431
Oh, my God.
Meg's in love with Tom Tucker!

10:03.766 --> 10:07.020
Try to move in on my woman,
will you, Tom Tucker?

10:07.103 --> 10:10.774
No one crosses Neil Goldman
and gets away with it.

10:10.774 --> 10:14.527
I added something to your coffee
I don't think you're gonna like.

10:14.527 --> 10:18.696
- Here's your coffee, Mr Tucker.
- What the hell is in this?

10:18.780 --> 10:21.700
Sweet'N Low.
That's for trying to steal my woman!

10:21.825 --> 10:24.953
- Bring it to me with urine in it like I asked.
- Yes, sir.

10:28.916 --> 10:32.460
- Nice bike.
- That's the understatement of the century.

10:32.544 --> 10:37.340
- It's cool. Too cool for you.
- No, no. I think it's right where I'm at.

10:37.465 --> 10:38.592
Out of my way!

10:38.717 --> 10:43.720
Oh, I see. Oh, yes, I suppose you do have
to ride it to truly appreciate its virtues.

10:43.805 --> 10:47.349
Well, then, I'll just wait
right here till you get back.

10:48.518 --> 10:52.354
- Where the devil is he?
- You've obviously never met a bully.

10:52.479 --> 10:53.816
What do you mean?

10:53.941 --> 10:57.275
He wasn't taking it for a test ride,
he was just taking it.

10:57.275 --> 10:59.654
- You... you mean...?
- Mm-hm.

10:59.780 --> 11:03.616
He... stole... my trikey?

11:09.663 --> 11:12.708
Mr Tucker, has anyone
ever told you your eyes are...

11:12.708 --> 11:17.296
Hang on, sweetie. I've gotta call Peter
Jennings and reschedule our golf game.

11:28.974 --> 11:31.683
This is Peter. You know what to do.

11:31.683 --> 11:36.563
Mr Tucker, Miss Simmons, there's a nut on
top of Town Hall with a high-powered rifle.

11:36.688 --> 11:40.943
The gunman's been identified as the
Mass Media Murderer who targets the press.

11:41.068 --> 11:43.863
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Mass Media Murderer?

11:43.988 --> 11:48.783
I think this would be a fine opportunity
to give our interns real-world experience.

11:48.867 --> 11:52.829
That means you'll get to ride
in the news chopper. I'm so jealous.

11:52.954 --> 11:56.166
Better put in for some new interns.
Good luck!

11:56.291 --> 11:58.042
I've got Hugh Downs up here.

11:58.168 --> 12:01.921
I'm gonna splatter his distinguished career
all over the pavement.

12:01.921 --> 12:04.926
- Hey, why me? Why the media?
- I've got my reasons.

12:05.051 --> 12:09.304
Dan Rather thinks he can condense
a whole day's events into a half-hour.

12:09.429 --> 12:12.224
Don't get me started on that arrogant jerk.

12:12.349 --> 12:15.769
- Really? You know him?
- I'm Hugh Downs. I know everybody.

12:15.893 --> 12:18.479
- In fact, he's down there.
- Where?

12:18.604 --> 12:23.402
Ha-ha! See ya later, sucker! And by the way,
Rather is an OK guy in small doses.

12:25.571 --> 12:27.572
Look how close we're getting, Meg.

12:28.615 --> 12:30.992
Hey! That was my lucky assassin hat!

12:33.410 --> 12:35.580
Mayday! Mayday! I'm going down!

12:40.585 --> 12:44.880
Oh, my God, we're gonna die! There's
so much of life I haven't experienced!

12:44.963 --> 12:48.717
I never got the chance to be some
drunk college guy's last resort!

12:48.842 --> 12:52.180
My years of expensive orthodontic work
will be a total waste!

12:52.263 --> 12:57.060
- I never even had my first kiss!
- It's not too late, Meg.

12:59.769 --> 13:02.063
I'm here for you.

13:04.483 --> 13:07.401
Time to sign off.

13:08.527 --> 13:10.822
Remember me, dirt bag?

13:35.346 --> 13:37.848
Wow! You saved
those kids' lives, Mr Downs.

13:37.931 --> 13:40.226
All in a day's work. If you ever need me,

13:40.351 --> 13:43.562
just blow this whistle,
or call John Stossel's cellphone.

13:43.687 --> 13:46.398
Hugh Downs away!

13:48.065 --> 13:51.069
Honey, thank God you're safe.
We were so worried.

13:51.194 --> 13:53.364
We now go to junior anchor Neil Goldman

13:53.489 --> 13:56.700
with exclusive footage
from today's exciting scene.

13:56.825 --> 14:00.786
Thank you, Diane. There may have been
some commotion on the rooftop,

14:00.869 --> 14:06.001
but the real story was inside the mouths
of Meg Griffin and Neil Goldman,

14:06.084 --> 14:09.546
where a meeting of the tongues,
a summit of saliva,

14:09.630 --> 14:13.383
established a new world order of love.

14:13.508 --> 14:14.424
Agh!

14:17.553 --> 14:20.056
Let's watch it one more time
in super slow-mo.

14:20.181 --> 14:23.310
This is where we cease to be Meg and Neil

14:23.394 --> 14:26.645
and begin life anew as Meil.

14:26.729 --> 14:28.940
Oh, my God. He put it on TV?

14:29.024 --> 14:32.276
Isn't that cute, Peter?
Our daughter's first love.

14:32.360 --> 14:38.198
I just want to kill myself! I'm going upstairs
right now and eat a whole bowl of peanuts.

14:38.323 --> 14:40.283
I'm allergic to peanuts!

14:41.743 --> 14:44.995
You don't know anything about me!

14:44.995 --> 14:46.248
Who was that guy?

14:47.998 --> 14:51.044
Constable, I'd like to report
the theft of my tricycle.

14:51.128 --> 14:56.466
Oh, look at the little baby.
Aren't you cute! Where's your mommy?

14:56.549 --> 14:59.677
How dare you condescend to me?
I demand justice!

14:59.802 --> 15:04.599
I'm here to turn myself in. I have
a dismembered hooker bleeding in my trunk.

15:04.682 --> 15:09.895
Oh, look at the little baby.
Aren't you cute! Where's your mommy?

15:21.157 --> 15:23.658
- Where did you get that shirt?
- From Neil.

15:23.783 --> 15:25.119
Hello, lover.

15:25.244 --> 15:29.290
Neil, what are you doing?
I'm not your lover. I don't even like you.

15:29.415 --> 15:33.585
Meg, I strongly suggest you hold
my hand, lest you look like a slut.

15:33.668 --> 15:37.338
Tell these people that there's
nothing going on between us.

15:37.338 --> 15:41.509
Oh, don't be afraid of the fire, Meg.
I won't let you burn.

15:43.386 --> 15:45.055
Al, why haven't I leaped?

15:45.138 --> 15:48.056
Ziggy says you can't leap
until she loves you back.

15:48.182 --> 15:49.517
Don't worry, I'll get her.

15:51.520 --> 15:54.104
What do you want to work on?
Cardio? Upper body?

15:54.229 --> 15:57.566
Upper body. I need to get buff,
so I can get my tricycle back.

15:57.566 --> 16:01.403
Luckily, we're running a special
for the next 17 minutes.

16:01.528 --> 16:04.866
OK. That's a little unusual but... OK, tell me.

16:04.866 --> 16:08.703
The normal plan is 78 months
at 40 a month and 200 down. Watch this.

16:08.828 --> 16:10.371
- Forget the down.
- Yeah.

16:10.496 --> 16:12.371
Goodbye 40 a month, let's do 35.

16:12.455 --> 16:15.709
- 35. That's the cheapest?
- Yeah, hang on, hang on.

16:15.792 --> 16:18.211
Trace, can you bring me
some free gym bags?

16:18.295 --> 16:20.923
I could probably just do
some push-ups at home.

16:21.006 --> 16:24.468
Let's start you off with a body-fat test,
maybe a heart rate.

16:24.468 --> 16:28.221
You're not hearing me. I don't think
this is for me. Thanks, anyway.

16:28.305 --> 16:32.475
And for the future,
you came on a little strong.

16:36.771 --> 16:40.317
- What's going on here?
- We invited Neil's family over for dinner.

16:40.400 --> 16:41.567
- Hi.
- Hello.

16:41.650 --> 16:43.945
- You what?!
- To get to know 'em better.

16:44.070 --> 16:46.364
Seeing as you two
will one day bless our home

16:46.447 --> 16:49.575
with the pitter-patter
of grandchildren as ugly as sin.

16:49.700 --> 16:52.912
Meg, you never told me your mother
was such a stone-cold fox.

16:53.037 --> 16:56.791
- Now I see where you get it.
- Meg, he's so charming.

16:56.791 --> 16:58.750
My name is Chris.

16:58.875 --> 17:03.673
I'm supposed to be on my best behaviour
tonight and not mention poo.

17:03.756 --> 17:06.258
Oh, God, what have I done?!

17:06.383 --> 17:08.551
Well, let's eat.

17:08.676 --> 17:12.847
I think it's very, very nice that our children
had this wonderful kiss.

17:12.932 --> 17:17.309
I remember when Muriel and I had
our first kiss, and it was just awful.

17:17.434 --> 17:22.230
Oh, just awful. We were both very sick.
Weren't we, dear?

17:22.316 --> 17:24.318
Ugh, we were terribly sick.

17:24.401 --> 17:29.196
We were both 14 and it was winter
and we had terrible head colds.

17:29.321 --> 17:34.743
Mine especially was very bad. I had terrible
mucus coming out from inside my nose.

17:34.826 --> 17:37.872
And the other children,
they were very nasty to me.

17:37.955 --> 17:40.167
They said bad, hurtful things to me.

17:40.251 --> 17:41.917
They called me Tasty Cakes,

17:42.042 --> 17:45.797
and they would beat me
and stick pine cones in my ass.

17:45.879 --> 17:49.967
- Those were very bad times.
- I'm sorry to hear that.

17:50.050 --> 17:51.844
Thank you very much.

17:51.844 --> 17:54.221
Excuse me. I'm gonna go throw up.

17:54.346 --> 17:56.931
Please flush the toilet twice.

17:57.056 --> 18:01.646
Once for the bulk, and again for the
remainder. Thank you. Oh, she's a dear.

18:04.856 --> 18:07.276
You're blocking my light, you stupid baby!

18:07.359 --> 18:10.278
My hooligan friend,
I've been racking my brain

18:10.403 --> 18:13.531
in a fruitless attempt
to resolve our unpleasantness.

18:13.614 --> 18:18.745
But then it dawned on me. Your cruelty
merely stems from a deep-seated inner pain.

18:18.828 --> 18:21.956
The obvious remedy
is a healthy dose of outer pain!

18:25.834 --> 18:30.422
Children washing cars to raise money
for charity. Is anything more arousing?

18:30.422 --> 18:36.470
We go to Meg Griffin for a special Channel
Five junior anchor segment on the moon.

18:36.553 --> 18:41.684
The moon. There's a reason
no one goes there. It's cold, and it's ugly.

18:41.767 --> 18:45.021
Its surface is plagued
with craters and jagged peaks.

18:45.021 --> 18:50.108
Oh, wait! That's not the moon.
It's Neil Goldman's face.

18:50.234 --> 18:53.777
Recently, many of you saw me
kissing this freak of nature.

18:53.861 --> 18:57.114
If I wasn't seconds away from death,
I wouldn't have done it.

18:57.114 --> 19:01.578
I mean, who in their right mind would?
I went to the streets to find out.

19:01.703 --> 19:03.246
Would you kiss this guy?

19:03.372 --> 19:05.248
- Ugh! No!
- No way!

19:05.331 --> 19:07.334
- No!
- No!

19:07.417 --> 19:10.336
Oh, God, no!
What's the matter with you? Oh!

19:10.461 --> 19:13.173
It's official. Neil Goldman isn't kissable.

19:13.256 --> 19:16.926
Hear that, Neil? I don't like you.
I never will! Back to you, Tom.

19:16.926 --> 19:20.764
Thank you, Meg. I guess beggars
can be choosers. And now this.

19:22.847 --> 19:27.771
- Well, well. Isn't this a darling picture!
- Let me go, man!

19:27.771 --> 19:30.148
- How old are you, Charlie?
- Seven.

19:30.273 --> 19:33.693
Seven? Well, my, my.
You're practically a lady.

19:33.818 --> 19:36.737
Ironic that your fate
is in the hands of an infant.

19:36.737 --> 19:40.907
- Now tell me where my tricycle is!
- I don't know. I lost it.

19:40.991 --> 19:44.661
- Agh!
- I have other ways of obtaining the truth.

19:46.330 --> 19:48.290
No! Don't!

19:48.915 --> 19:53.002
- Stewie? Look what I found.
- My trikey!

19:53.085 --> 19:56.215
- What's going on down here?
- We're playing house.

19:56.340 --> 19:58.424
That boy is all tied up.

19:59.676 --> 20:01.428
Roman Polanski's house.

20:02.887 --> 20:07.391
Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.
Our top story: The president has been shot.

20:07.474 --> 20:10.936
Tragedy strikes the nation.
The president has been shot.

20:11.019 --> 20:14.358
Why's the president in this casket?
We'll tell you.

20:14.483 --> 20:18.026
- Nice job on that report last night.
- Wow! Thanks, Mr Tucker.

20:18.111 --> 20:21.154
That means so much coming
from someone so handsome.

20:21.238 --> 20:26.661
- How'd you like to pick up my dry-cleaning?
- Sure. But isn't that Neil's job?

20:26.786 --> 20:29.705
- Little jerk hasn't been in all day.
- He hasn't?

20:29.705 --> 20:33.541
A breaking story! A geek is on top of
Town Hall! He's about to jump!

20:35.126 --> 20:37.921
- Oh, my God! Neil!
- Is it Neil?

20:38.046 --> 20:40.339
I've been calling him Ned all week.

20:41.590 --> 20:43.678
Oh, my God! Neil, please don't jump.

20:43.761 --> 20:49.099
I was just a piece of eye candy
that she turned into an all-day sucker.

20:53.269 --> 20:57.648
Mr Tucker! Thank God you're here!
Someone's got to do something! He'll fall!

20:57.648 --> 21:03.279
I'm on it. Have that cartoon sound-effect
guy cue up the...

21:03.363 --> 21:05.448
Top it off with a...

21:05.573 --> 21:09.619
And if there's time, be ready with a...
"Wah, wah, wah, wah.

21:09.744 --> 21:12.329
You don't care about him at all, do you?

21:12.455 --> 21:16.416
All you care about are your stupid ratings!
You're a horrible man!

21:16.499 --> 21:19.128
- Neil, I'm sorry!
- Meg?

21:20.670 --> 21:24.132
- There he goes!
- Good stuff, good stuff, good stuff!

21:24.216 --> 21:26.843
Neil!

21:26.927 --> 21:31.223
- Meg! You do care!
- Don't read too much into this, Neil.

21:31.223 --> 21:34.976
It's hard not to when I'm lying
right on top of you.

21:35.060 --> 21:39.646
Just because you're repulsive and
the most annoying person on the planet,

21:39.771 --> 21:44.026
and I'm not the only one who thinks so,
doesn't mean I want you to kill yourself.

21:44.150 --> 21:47.780
Thanks, Meg. But I was never
really planning to jump.

21:47.906 --> 21:50.617
Wasn't gonna jump? You're a phony!

21:50.700 --> 21:54.371
Hey, everybody!
This guy's a great big phony!

21:54.372 --> 22:55.372
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru